    "reply": "I added `tests/test_payments.py` with 12 `unittest` tests covering `line_total`, `order_total` and `refund` in `shop/payments.py`. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passes, and I didn't touch anything under `shop/`.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- **`line_total`:** multiplication, zero quantity, and a float price.\n- **`order_total`:** an empty order, a single line with tax, several lines summed before tax, rounding to cents, a known value (100 \u2192 108.25), and zero-priced items.\n- **`refund`:** a partial refund, a full refund leaving zero, and a zero refund.\n\nI didn't mark anything `expectedFailure` because I didn't find a clear bug. Two things you may want to decide on, which I did not test as bugs because the module has no spec for them:\n- `refund` doesn't reject an amount larger than the order total, so it can return a negative balance.\n- `line_total` and `order_total` don't reject negative prices or quantities.\n\nTell me the intended behavior and I can add those as tests, marking them `expectedFailure` if the code disagrees.",
